I borrowed the yellow disc for the headline, with the first line in black and the second in cobalt. The short description of what I do sits on a black ribbon: “Platforms. Content. People. Connected by design.” A red diagonal sits behind the blue project card.

The squiggles, triangles and serrated edges were fun to work with. Some turned up around code blocks and quotations too, with the decoration kept out of the text itself.

The homepage headline uses [Science Gothic](https://github.com/googlefonts/science-gothic). Its letterforms already lean, so I kept the baseline level and left the rotation to the ribbon and project plate. The homepage uses a small, fixed subset rather than the complete variable font.

## Give the introduction something to point at

The homepage still needs to explain what I do. Beside “Make it make sense”, I've put a project card linking to [my work at UNDRR connecting Storybook, structured content, design tokens, and Figma](/work/2026/impact-story-mangrove-figma/). It pulls its title, image and description from the published entry.

Below that are the six latest entries, under “Ideas in circulation”, with dates, short descriptions and thumbnails. The links to writing, work, my profile and search are still at the top.

## A second reference: fragments on paper

I also had a TurboGrafx-16 growing up and loved it and its personality. [This ad in *Electronic Gaming Monthly*](https://archives.tg-16.com/EGM_1989_07.htm) caught my eye too: a face and game screenshots cut into odd shapes, with bits of red and yellow overlapping them. There is a lot happening, but also a surprising amount of empty paper.

