TurboGrafx advertising ranged from sophisticated to childish. [Christian Nutt's oral history](https://www.gamedeveloper.com/business/stalled-engine-the-turbografx-16-turns-25) follows the change from NEC to Turbo Technologies Inc. (TTI), including the later Johnny Turbo comic-book ads. What I wanted from this particular spread was the fractured photograph, the sharp cuts and the space around the pieces.

The [cut-paper collage study](/design-lab/collage/) applies that composition to a screenshot of the Mangrove Figma library, with cropped details and a black shape behind it. The whole screenshot is still there to look at.

